# shell: desktop
# TS-063/TS-001/TS-008: the desktop shell's column strip answers gestures --
# a click sorts, a second click reverses, a title dragged out of the strip
# tears the column off behind a dotted outline, and a drag that returns
# puts it back; right-clicking the strip opens the Attributes menu.
wait 10
note clicking the Name title reverses the sort: the files flip to c,b,a
click 100 96
wait 4
click-row 3
wait 2
expect-selected-name a.txt
wait 40
note clicking it again puts them back ascending
click 100 96
wait 4
click-row 3
wait 2
expect-selected-name c.txt
note a column dragged out of the strip is torn off behind a dotted outline
expect-columns 4
press 340 96
move 340 130
move 340 200
wait 2
expect-pixel 270 190 000000
note but a drag that RETURNS to the strip puts the column back
move 340 130
move 340 96
release 340 96
wait 3
expect-columns 4
note dragged out and released, the removal stands
press 340 96
move 340 130
move 340 200
release 340 200
wait 3
expect-columns 3
note right-clicking the strip opens the Attributes menu in place
click 200 96 3
wait 3
expect-menu Kind
quit
